<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST-Autoliv 9-mo seen 870 mln skr.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Autoliv 9-mo seen 870 mln skr.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish car safety equipment manufacturer Autoliv is expected to show a pre-tax profit of 870 million crowns for the first nine months of the year, a Reuter poll of eight analysts found on Monday.</p>
<p>This would represent a 15 percent improvement on the earnings of 758 million crowns posted for the corresponding period last year.</p>
<p>The average forecast for the full year put Autoliv's earnings at 1.18 billion crowns, compared with the 1.01 billion reported for 1995.</p>
<p>Sales for the first three quarters are seen at 8.55 billion crowns, rising to 11.56 billion for the year.</p>
<p>The dividend paid for 1996 is estimated at 3.11 crowns per share, up from 2.25 crowns. However, forecasts for the dividend range from 2.50 crowns to 5.50.</p>
<p>Autoliv is due to publish its nine-month results on October 28.</p>
<p>  (Mkr)		Average	   Range		Analysts</p>
<p> Profit, 9-mo 96	870		848-900	     8</p>
<p> Profit, 1996	 1,179	  1,125-1,205	     8</p>
<p> Profit, 1997	 1,372	  1,260-1,500	     7</p>
<p> Profit, 1998	 1,577	  1,400-1,800	     7</p>
<p> Sales, 9-mo 96     8,552	  8,325-8,950	     8</p>
<p> Sales, 1996	 11,556	 11,100-12,200	    8</p>
<p> Sales, 1997	 13,169	 12,200-13,983	    7</p>
<p> Sales, 1998	 14,810	 13,000-16,007	    7</p>
<p> Dividend 96 (SKR)   3.11	   2.50-5.50		7</p>
<p> Dividend 97 (SKR)   3.94	   3.00-6.50		6</p>
<p> Dividend 98 (SKR)   4.42	   3.50-7.00		6</p>
